# Unity/C# Coding Standards

## Naming Conventions

### Classes and Public Members
- **Classes**: PascalCase (e.g., `LabyrinthGame`, `GenerateGameScene`)
- **Public methods**: PascalCase (e.g., `LoadLevel`, `UI_Continue`)
- **Public fields**: PascalCase (e.g., `mainMenuCanvas`, `moveSpeed`)

### Private Members
- **Private fields**: Prefix with underscore `_` (e.g., `_cc`, `_playerRoot`, `_isPaused`)
- **Private methods**: PascalCase (e.g., `UpdateMovement`, `CreateWallAtWorld`)
- **Local variables**: camelCase (e.g., `delta`, `mv`, `dir`)

### Constants
- **Constants**: PascalCase with `const` keyword (e.g., `const string PendingKey = "LG_PendingGenerate"`)

## Unity-Specific Patterns

### MonoBehaviour Lifecycle
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Proper lifecycle order
private void Awake()
{
    // Initialize references, create objects
}

private void OnEnable()
{
    // Enable input actions, subscribe to events
}

private void OnDisable()
{
    // Disable input actions, unsubscribe from events
}

private void Update()
{
    // Per-frame logic
}
```

### Serialized Fields
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Use [Header] for organization
[Header("Параметры игрока")]
public float moveSpeed = 8f;
public float lookSensitivity = 0.12f;

[Header("Аудио (WebGL: wav/ogg)")]
public AudioClip footstepLoop;
public AudioClip backgroundMusic;
```

### Component References
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Cache component references
private CharacterController _cc;
private Camera _cam;

private void Awake()
{
    _cc = GetComponent<CharacterController>();
    _cam = GetComponentInChildren<Camera>(true);
}

// ❌ BAD: Don't call GetComponent every frame
private void Update()
{
    GetComponent<CharacterController>().Move(direction); // BAD!
}
```

### GameObject Creation
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Set parent immediately, use meaningful names
GameObject wall = new GameObject($"Wall_{wallId}");
wall.transform.SetParent(parent, false);
wall.name = "WallSegment";

// ✅ GOOD: Use CreatePrimitive when appropriate
GameObject floor = GameObject.CreatePrimitive(PrimitiveType.Quad);
floor.name = "Floor";
```

