## Code Organization

### Method Ordering
1. Unity lifecycle methods (`Awake`, `OnEnable`, `Start`, `Update`, etc.)
2. Public methods (UI handlers, public API)
3. Private helper methods (grouped by functionality)

### Using Directives
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Group and organize usings
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI;
using UnityEngine.InputSystem;

#if UNITY_EDITOR
using UnityEditor;
#endif
```

## Error Handling

### Null Checks
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Check for null before using Unity objects
if (_cam == null || _playerRoot == null) return;

if (mainMenuCanvas != null) 
    mainMenuCanvas.gameObject.SetActive(visible);

// ✅ GOOD: Use null-conditional operator when appropriate
_moveAction?.Enable();
_footstepsSource?.Stop();
```

### Debug Logging
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Use Debug.Log for important events
Debug.Log("LoadLevel " + levelIndex);

// ✅ GOOD: Use Debug.LogError for critical issues
Debug.LogError("URP Lit shader not found. Check URP setup.");
```

## Performance Best Practices

### Avoid Allocations in Update
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Cache collections and reuse
private readonly Dictionary<Sprite, Mesh> _spriteMeshCache = new Dictionary<Sprite, Mesh>();

// ❌ BAD: Don't allocate every frame
private void Update()
{
    var list = new List<Vector3>(); // BAD!
}
```

### Use Object Pooling for Frequent Instantiation
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Consider pooling for frequently created/destroyed objects
// For example, graffiti objects could be pooled
```

### Efficient Raycasting
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Use appropriate raycast distance
Ray r = new Ray(_cam.transform.position, _cam.transform.forward);
if (!Physics.Raycast(r, out RaycastHit hit, 500f)) return;
```

## Input System

### Input Actions
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Create InputActions programmatically
private InputAction _moveAction;
private InputAction _lookAction;

private void CreateInputActions()
{
    _moveAction = new InputAction("Move", InputActionType.Value, null, null, null, "Vector2");
    _moveAction.AddCompositeBinding("2DVector")
        .With("Up", "<Keyboard>/w")
        .With("Down", "<Keyboard>/s");
}

private void OnEnable()
{
    _moveAction?.Enable();
}

private void OnDisable()
{
    _moveAction?.Disable();
}
```

## Material and Shader Handling

### URP Shader Access
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Find shader and handle null case
Shader lit = Shader.Find("Universal Render Pipeline/Lit");
if (lit == null)
{
    Debug.LogError("URP Lit shader not found.");
    return;
}

Material mat = new Material(lit);
```

### Material Properties
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Check for property existence before setting
if (mat.HasProperty("_BaseColor"))
    mat.SetColor("_BaseColor", Color.white);
if (mat.HasProperty("_BaseMap"))
    mat.SetTexture("_BaseMap", texture);
```

